   "source": [
    "## 4. Output contract\n",
    "\n",
    "The core methodological fix. Both the chain and the baseline must end with the\n",
    "same JSON block. Without this you cannot grade anything automatically, and any\n",
    "\"improvement\" you report is just your own reading of two paragraphs of prose.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Fairness note for interviews:** the baseline gets the *identical* contract.\n",
    "If you gave the chain a stricter format than the baseline, any difference in\n",
    "score could just be the formatting instruction, not the chaining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "OUTPUT_CONTRACT = \"\"\"\n",
    "End your response with a single JSON object and nothing after it, in exactly this form:\n",
    "\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"q1_value\": <number>,\n",
    "  \"q2_label\": \"<short name>\",\n",
    "  \"q2_value\": <number>,\n",
    "  \"q3_label\": \"<short name>\",\n",
    "  \"q3_value\": <number>\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules: numbers only, no currency symbols, no thousands separators, no units,\n",
    "no percent signs. Labels must be the short name only (for example \"B\", \"Large\",\n",
    "\"GenAI\"), not a sentence.\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def build_decomposition_prompt(problem: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return f\"\"\"You are an expert analytical problem solver.\n",
    "\n",
    "Break the problem below into a numbered list of sequential sub-tasks. Each\n",
    "sub-task must be specific and independently solvable. Do NOT solve anything yet.\n",
    "\n",
    "PROBLEM:\n",
    "{problem}\n",
    "\n",
    "SUB-TASKS:\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_solver_prompt(problem: str, subtasks: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return f\"\"\"You are an expert quantitative reasoning assistant.\n",
    "\n",
    "Solve each sub-task below step by step. Show every calculation. Label each\n",
    "solution with its sub-task number. Be exact with numbers.\n",
    "\n",
    "PROBLEM:\n",
    "{problem}\n",
    "\n",
    "SUB-TASKS:\n",
    "{subtasks}\n",
    "\n",
    "STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTIONS:\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_synthesis_prompt(problem: str, solutions: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return f\"\"\"You are a senior business analyst writing a final answer.\n",
    "\n",
    "PROBLEM:\n",
    "{problem}\n",
    "\n",
    "INTERMEDIATE WORKINGS:\n",
    "{solutions}\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer Q1, Q2 and Q3 in order, briefly.\n",
    "{OUTPUT_CONTRACT}\n",
    "\n",
    "FINAL ANSWER:\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_single_shot_prompt(problem: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return f\"\"\"Solve the following problem completely and answer all three questions.\n",
    "\n",
    "{problem}\n",
    "\n",
    "{OUTPUT_CONTRACT}\n",
    "\n",
    "ANSWER:\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Prompt builders defined.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Parsing and grading\n",
    "\n",
    "`parse_answer` tries strict JSON first, then falls back to regex. If both fail\n",
    "it returns `None` — and that counts as a **parse failure**, tracked separately.\n",
    "Do not let a parse failure silently score as zero without recording why; you\n",
    "need to know whether the model was wrong or merely unformatted."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def parse_answer(text: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract the answer dict from raw model output. Returns None if unparseable.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if not text:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Strategy 1: last JSON object in the text\n",
    "    candidates = re.findall(r\"\\{[^{}]*\\}\", text, re.DOTALL)\n",
    "    for block in reversed(candidates):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            obj = json.loads(block)\n",
    "            if any(k in obj for k in ANSWER_KEYS):\n",
    "                return obj\n",
    "        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Strategy 2: regex per key, for models that ignore the contract\n",
    "    obj = {}\n",
    "    for key in ANSWER_KEYS:\n",
    "        m = re.search(rf'\"?{key}\"?\\s*[:=]\\s*\"?([^\",\\n}}]+)\"?', text)\n",
    "        if m:\n",
    "            obj[key] = m.group(1).strip()\n",
    "    return obj if obj else None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _to_float(v: Any) -> Optional[float]:\n",
    "    if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n",
    "        return float(v)\n",
    "    if not isinstance(v, str):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    cleaned = re.sub(r\"[^\\d.\\-]\", \"\", v.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return float(cleaned)\n",
    "    except ValueError:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _norm_label(v: Any) -> str:\n",
    "    s = str(v).lower().strip()\n",
    "    s = re.sub(r\"^(product|tier|size|program|the)\\s+\", \"\", s)\n",
    "    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9 ]\", \"\", s).strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def grade_field(key: str, predicted: Any, expected: Any) -> bool:\n",
    "    if predicted is None:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    if key.endswith(\"_label\"):\n",
    "        p, e = _norm_label(predicted), _norm_label(expected)\n",
    "        return p == e or re.search(rf\"\\b{re.escape(e)}\\b\", p) is not None\n",
    "    p = _to_float(predicted)\n",
    "    if p is None:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    e = float(expected)\n",
    "    tol = max(abs(e) * 0.005, 0.05)   # 0.5% relative, small absolute floor\n",
    "    return abs(p - e) <= tol\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def grade(parsed: Optional[Dict[str, Any]], ground_truth: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
    "    if parsed is None:\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"parse_ok\": False, \"fields_correct\": 0, \"fields_total\": len(ANSWER_KEYS),\n",
    "            \"field_accuracy\": 0.0, \"fully_correct\": False,\n",
    "            \"per_field\": {k: False for k in ANSWER_KEYS},\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    per_field = {k: grade_field(k, parsed.get(k), ground_truth[k]) for k in ANSWER_KEYS}\n",
    "    correct = sum(per_field.values())\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"parse_ok\": True, \"fields_correct\": correct, \"fields_total\": len(ANSWER_KEYS),\n",
    "        \"field_accuracy\": correct / len(ANSWER_KEYS),\n",
    "        \"fully_correct\": correct == len(ANSWER_KEYS),\n",
    "        \"per_field\": per_field,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "_rouge = rouge_scorer.RougeScorer([\"rouge1\", \"rouge2\", \"rougeL\"], use_stemmer=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def rouge_scores(prediction: str, reference: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n",
    "    s = _rouge.score(reference, prediction or \"\")\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"rouge1\": round(s[\"rouge1\"].fmeasure, 4),\n",
    "        \"rouge2\": round(s[\"rouge2\"].fmeasure, 4),\n",
    "        \"rougeL\": round(s[\"rougeL\"].fmeasure, 4),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Grader defined.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. The chain\n",
    "\n",
    "Same 3 stages as v1, but it keeps every intermediate output so you can see\n",
    "**where** the chain broke. This matters: a chain can fail at step 1 and still\n",
    "produce confident-looking output at step 3. That is error propagation, and it\n",
    "is the main structural weakness of naive prompt chaining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MultiStepReasoningChain:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Decompose -> solve -> synthesize.\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, llm: LLMWrapper, verbose: bool = False):\n",
    "        self.llm = llm\n",
    "        self.verbose = verbose\n",
    "\n",
    "    def run(self, problem: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
    "        t0 = time.time()\n",
    "\n",
    "        p1 = build_decomposition_prompt(problem)\n",
    "        subtasks = self.llm.generate(p1, max_tokens=400, temperature=0.0)\n",
    "        if self.verbose:\n",
    "            print(f\"[1/3] decomposed ({len(subtasks.split())} words)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        p2 = build_solver_prompt(problem, subtasks)\n",
    "        solutions = self.llm.generate(p2, max_tokens=700, temperature=0.0)\n",
    "        if self.verbose:\n",
    "            print(f\"[2/3] solved ({len(solutions.split())} words)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        p3 = build_synthesis_prompt(problem, solutions)\n",
    "        final = self.llm.generate(p3, max_tokens=500, temperature=0.0)\n",
    "        if self.verbose:\n",
    "            print(f\"[3/3] synthesized ({len(final.split())} words)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"subtasks\": subtasks,\n",
    "            \"solutions\": solutions,\n",
    "            \"final_answer\": final,\n",
    "            \"llm_calls\": 3,\n",
    "            \"seconds\": round(time.time() - t0, 2),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_single_shot(llm: LLMWrapper, problem: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
    "    t0 = time.time()\n",
    "    out = llm.generate(build_single_shot_prompt(problem), max_tokens=700, temperature=0.0)\n",
    "    return {\"final_answer\": out, \"llm_calls\": 1, \"seconds\": round(time.time() - t0, 2)}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Chain defined.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Experiment runner"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_experiment(llm: LLMWrapper, eval_set: List[Dict[str, Any]], verbose: bool = True):\n",
    "    chain = MultiStepReasoningChain(llm, verbose=False)\n",
    "    rows, transcripts = [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for prob in eval_set:\n",
    "        if verbose:\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n--- {prob['id']} ---\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        for method, runner in [(\"single_shot\", lambda p: run_single_shot(llm, p)),\n",
    "                               (\"chain\", lambda p: chain.run(p))]:\n",
    "            res = runner(prob[\"text\"])\n",
    "            parsed = parse_answer(res[\"final_answer\"])\n",
    "            g = grade(parsed, prob[\"ground_truth\"])\n",
    "            r = rouge_scores(res[\"final_answer\"], prob[\"reference_text\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "            rows.append({\n",
    "                \"problem\": prob[\"id\"], \"method\": method, \"model\": llm.describe(),\n",
    "                \"parse_ok\": g[\"parse_ok\"], \"field_accuracy\": g[\"field_accuracy\"],\n",
    "                \"fully_correct\": g[\"fully_correct\"], \"llm_calls\": res[\"llm_calls\"],\n",
    "                \"seconds\": res[\"seconds\"], **r,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "            transcripts.append({\"problem\": prob[\"id\"], \"method\": method,\n",
    "                                \"parsed\": parsed, \"grade\": g, \"raw\": res})\n",
    "            if verbose:\n",
    "                flag = \"ok\" if g[\"parse_ok\"] else \"PARSE FAIL\"\n",
    "                print(f\"  {method:12s} acc={g['field_accuracy']:.2f}  \"\n",
    "                      f\"exact={g['fully_correct']}  rougeL={r['rougeL']:.3f}  [{flag}]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows), transcripts\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "results_df, transcripts = run_experiment(llm, EVAL_SET)\n",
    "results_df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Results summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the two metrics against each other. If ROUGE ranks the methods\n",
    "differently from exact-match accuracy, say so explicitly — that disagreement\n",
    "is the most interesting finding available from this notebook, and it is the\n",
    "thing worth talking about in an interview."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary = (results_df\n",
    "           .groupby([\"model\", \"method\"])\n",
    "           .agg(field_accuracy=(\"field_accuracy\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                exact_solve_rate=(\"fully_correct\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                parse_success=(\"parse_ok\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                rougeL=(\"rougeL\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                avg_llm_calls=(\"llm_calls\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                avg_seconds=(\"seconds\", \"mean\"))\n",
    "           .round(3)\n",
    "           .reset_index())\n",
    "\n",
    "display(Markdown(\"### Summary: chain vs single-shot\"))\n",
    "display(summary)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Do the two metrics agree on which method is better?\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    by_method = summary.set_index(\"method\")\n",
    "    acc_winner = by_method[\"field_accuracy\"].idxmax()\n",
    "    rouge_winner = by_method[\"rougeL\"].idxmax()\n",
    "    if acc_winner != rouge_winner:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\nMETRICS DISAGREE: accuracy favours '{acc_winner}', \"\n",
    "              f\"ROUGE-L favours '{rouge_winner}'.\")\n",
    "        print(\"This is the evidence that ROUGE is a poor proxy for numeric correctness.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\nBoth metrics favour '{acc_winner}'.\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(\"Comparison skipped:\", e)"
   ]
  },
