    "## 11. Known limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep this section. Stating limits yourself is worth more in an interview than\n",
    "any headline number, and it stops you from over-claiming on a CV.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **n = 4.** Enough to avoid a single-anecdote conclusion, nowhere near enough\n",
    "   for statistical significance. Do not report a percentage improvement as if\n",
    "   it generalises.\n",
    "2. **One problem family.** All four are multi-step arithmetic on small business\n",
    "   scenarios. Results say nothing about code, retrieval, or open-ended reasoning.\n",
    "3. **Greedy decoding, single run.** `temperature=0.0` throughout, one sample per\n",
    "   condition. No variance estimate. Repeating each condition 3–5 times would be\n",
    "   the cheapest real improvement available.\n",
    "4. **Naive chaining.** No validation gate between stages, no retry, no\n",
    "   self-consistency. A wrong decomposition silently corrupts everything after it.\n",
    "5. **ROUGE is reported to be criticised, not trusted.** It is kept only to\n",
    "   demonstrate its inadequacy for numeric answers.\n",
    "6. **Ground truth is hand-computed by one person.** Unverified by anyone else.\n",
    "7. **Parsing is heuristic.** A model can be right in prose and still score zero\n",
    "   if it ignores the output contract. `parse_success` separates those cases —\n",
    "   always report it alongside accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## What you may honestly claim afterwards\n",
    "\n",
    "Only what your own executed output supports. In particular:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Claim the **backends you actually ran**, named correctly. If you never ran\n",
    "  Azure, the word Azure does not appear on your CV.\n",
    "- Claim **exact-match numeric accuracy and ROUGE** as your metrics.\n",
    "- Claim a **single-shot baseline comparison** — this is the part most junior\n",
    "  GenAI projects lack, and it is your real differentiator.\n",
    "- Do **not** claim LangChain, RAG, agents, fine-tuning, or deployment. None of\n",
    "  it is in this notebook.\n",
    "- If the chain underperforms, report that. A clean negative result you can\n",
    "  explain beats a vague positive one you cannot."
